<title>FRANCE: France's CAC-40 seen falling to 2,425 on left win.</title>
<headline>France's CAC-40 seen falling to 2,425 on left win.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's blue-chip CAC-40 index is expected to fall to 2,425 points if the combined left wins Sunday's parliamentary election and rally to 2,690 on a centre-right victory, according to a Reuter survey of 10 financial institutions on Friday.</p>
<p>The forecasts were for the week following the second round vote on Sunday.</p>
<p>The CAC-40 index closed at 2,583.94 on Friday.</p>
<p>Those surveyed said the CAC-40 could fall even further if the Socialist Party had to depend heavily on Communist Party support to form a government.</p>
<p>In a first round vote last Sunday the combined left led the ruling centre-right UDF/RPR coalition.</p>
<p>The institutions gave the following forecasts:</p>
<p>Levels of CAC-40 in the event of a centre-right or left majority in Sunday's parliamentary election.</p>
<p>			   Right     Left</p>
<p>Mean		     2,681     2,439</p>
<p>Median		   2,690     2,425</p>
<p>High		     2,750     2,525</p>
<p>Low			2,600     2,380</p>
<p>------------------------------------</p>
<p>Banque du Louvre     2,650     2,400</p>
<p>Banque Hottinguer    2,750     2,400</p>
<p>EIFB		     2,680     2,480</p>
<p>IFF			2,650     2,450</p>
<p>J Chahine		2,700     2,450</p>
<p>JP Morgan		2,600     2,400</p>
<p>Kleinwort Benson     2,700     2,525</p>
<p>UBS			2,675     2,500</p>
<p>unattributable	 2,700     2,380</p>
<p>unattributable	 2,700     2,400</p>
<p>-- Laura Geoffroy  Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
